  "cover_text": "Decreasing biodiversity in an ecosystem can increase the spread of invasive alien species. Due to climate change, the mayflies that lose the ability to reproduce can be unable to pollinate or fertilize other species. Given these facts, what decreases the spread of invasive alien species among reduced abiotic factors among corresponding choices:\n\n[i] Aphids\n[ii] Hoppers\n[iii] Predators\n[iv] Abrams\nThe answer is\n[i]Given information about the effects of drought, phosphorus concentration, and calcium concentrations on algae over a year in a lake ecosystem, Pyramid Lake could make a model to predict the year theoretical percent increases of algae over time.  Given the paragraph above, please answer correctly the following question:   Would an increase in phosphorus increase or decrease the percent changes in algae growth?\n",
